'''Richard Phillip Dickson''' (born November 17, 1987) is an American former [[college football|football]] player who was a [[tight end]] for the [[LSU Tigers football|LSU Tigers]] from 2005 to 2009.<ref>{{Cite web|url=http://louisianastate.scout.com/a.z?s=107&p=2&c=780288&ssf=1&RequestedURL=http%3a%2f%2flouisianastate.scout.com%2f2%2f780288.html|title = Geaux247 - LSU Tigers Football & Recruiting}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=Sun Herald:  Search Results |url=http://nl.newsbank.com/nl-search/we/Archives?p_product=BX&s_site=sunherald&p_multi=BX&p_theme=realcities&p_action=search&p_maxdocs=200&p_topdoc=1&p_text_direct-0=10DA4E0683056C18&p_field_direct-0=document_id&p_perpage=10&p_sort=YMD_date:D&s_trackval=GooglePM |archive-url=http://web.archive.org/web/20110609033646/http://nl.newsbank.com/nl-search/we/Archives?p_product=BX&s_site=sunherald&p_multi=BX&p_theme=realcities&p_action=search&p_maxdocs=200&p_topdoc=1&p_text_direct-0=10DA4E0683056C18&p_field_direct-0=document_id&p_perpage=10&p_sort=YMD_date:D&s_trackval=GooglePM |archive-date=2011-06-09 |access-date=2026-05-21 |website=nl.newsbank.com}}</ref><ref>[https://web.archive.org/web/20121102045434/http://pqasb.pqarchiver.com/washingtonpost/access/1409164081.html?dids=1409164081:1409164081&FMT=ABS&FMTS=ABS:FT&type=current&date=Jan+08,+2008&author=Eric+Prisbell+-+Washington+Post+Staff+Writer&pub=The+Washington+Post&desc=LSU+Takes+It+Big,+Easy%3B+Tigers+Put+Their+Two+Losses+Aside,+Rout+Ohio+State+to+Win+National+Title&pqatl=google Washington Post]</ref> He is the most productive tight end in school history with 90 [[Reception (American football)|receptions]] for 952 yards and 10 [[touchdown]]s.<ref>{{Cite web |url=http://www.lsusports.net/ViewArticle.dbml?SPSID=27812&SPID=2164&DB_LANG=C&DB_OEM_ID=5200&ATCLID=233464&Q_SEASON=2009 |title=LSU.net |access-date=September 1, 2010 |archive-date=June 16, 2011 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110616053050/http://www.lsusports.net/ViewArticle.dbml?SPSID=27812&SPID=2164&DB_LANG=C&DB_OEM_ID=5200&ATCLID=233464&Q_SEASON=2009 |url-status=dead }}</ref> In 2010, he was signed by the [[Detroit Lions]] as an [[undrafted free agent]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=Detroit Lions 2010 Roster Transactions |url=https://www.espn.com/nfl/team/transactions/_/name/det/season/2010 |access-date=2025-08-24 |website=ESPN.com |language=en}}</ref>

